 level. SUMLEV=40 appears to be the state level (I filtered for it).\n\nNow I need to create a build script that:\n1. Reads both data sources\n2. Filters census to SUMLEV=40 (state level)\n3. Joins on state name (farmers-markets.state_name == census.NAME)\n4. Sums the total farmers markets and total population\n5. Calculates the ratio per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me create this build script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HCgQ5r4eUhYYwGDsKsE85Y","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\", \n    con, \n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\", \n    con, \n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Filter census to state level (SUMLEV=40)\ncensus_states = census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 40)\n\n# Join on state name\njoined = fm.join(census_states, fm.state_name == census_states.NAME)\n\n# Aggregate total farmers markets and population\ntotals = joined.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum(),\n    total_population=census_states.POPESTIMATE2025.sum()\n)\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = totals.mutate(\n    farmers_markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / totals.total_population * 100000\n).select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"total_population\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input"